# Do not touch the protected core

## Context

`app/src/store.ts` (the dispatch/notify engine) and `app/src/types.ts` (core
types + the `Action` union) are load-bearing: changes ripple through the whole
app. Normal feature work extends `reducer.ts`/`actions.ts`, not these files.

## Rule

- Treat `app/src/store.ts` and `app/src/types.ts` as DO-NOT-TOUCH by default.
- NEVER edit the `createStore` dispatch/subscribe engine in `app/src/store.ts`.
- The ONLY sanctioned edit to `app/src/types.ts` is ADDING a new `Action`
  variant to the union (and, when a feature requires it, adding a field to an
  existing interface such as `Task`) — never remove or rename existing members.
- Do NOT change the public signatures of `createStore` or the action creators.
- If a task seems to require deeper changes to these files, STOP and ask the
  user for explicit approval first.

## How to verify

1. `git diff --stat app/src/store.ts` shows no changes for ordinary features.
2. Any diff to `app/src/types.ts` is additive (new union member / new field),
   never a removal or rename.
3. `createStore`, `getState`, `dispatch`, `subscribe` signatures are unchanged.

